cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "EB-CRISPR: guide RNA design for order-level bacterial enrichment"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Li"
    given-names: "Xiaolong"
    affiliation: "Florida State University"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/FSU-Li-Lab/EB-CRISPR"
url: "https://github.com/FSU-Li-Lab/EB-CRISPR"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline for designing dCas9 guide RNA panels that label an
  entire bacterial order, for cell-sorting-based enrichment from complex
  microbial communities. Handles the constraints specific to occupancy-based
  labelling assays: binding sites per genome rather than presence/absence,
  abundance-weighted off-target screening against a tiered negative set, and
  steric independence between guides. Applied to Enterobacterales, it produced
  a seven-guide panel giving a median of 31 binding sites per target genome
  with no off-targets across 32,536 background genomes.
keywords:
  - CRISPR
  - dCas9
  - guide RNA design
  - microbiome
  - Enterobacterales
  - cell sorting
  - comparative genomics
